{"results":[{"id":"6ab559662b978ca478cf0b21","name":"third-party.com Placeholder Domain Now Serves ClickFix","description":"The domain third-party[.]com, historically used as a documentation placeholder similar to example.com, has been compromised and now serves ClickFix lures to Windows users while displaying harmless content to other operating systems. Since at least June 2026, Windows visitors receive a fake Cloudflare verification page that poisons the clipboard with a malicious PowerShell command, instructing users to press Win+R and paste the payload. The domain appears in over 1,500 files across 1,700+ repositories from trusted sources including Chromium, Sanity, and Vercel. Unlike example.com, third-party[.]com is not IANA-reserved, allowing adversaries to register and weaponize it. The attack leverages social engineering to bypass security tools by using signed Windows binaries, making detection difficult through traditional scanning methods.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-09-24T19:51:28.883000","created":"2026-09-24T17:09:58.473000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4483055950,"indicator":"elxxvvx.xyz","type":"domain","created":"2026-09-24T17:09:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4507062071,"indicator":"http:\/\/elxxvvx.xyz\/f","type":"URL","created":"2026-09-24T17:09:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4507062072,"indicator":"http:\/\/elxxvvx.xyz\/f'","type":"URL","created":"2026-09-24T17:09:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4507062073,"indicator":"http:\/\/third-party.com\/token","type":"URL","created":"2026-09-24T17:09:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4507062074,"indicator":"http:\/\/third-party.com\/widget.js","type":"URL","created":"2026-09-24T17:09:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["clipboard poisoning","social engineering","powershell","fake captcha","third-party.com","placeholder domain","clickfix","windows targeting"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":[],"attack_ids":["T1218.011","T1204.002","T1566.002","T1082","T1071","T1053","T1106","T1140","T1218","T1027.001","T1059","T1204","T1059.001","T1566","T1027","T1071.001","T1105","T1204.001"],"references":["https:\/\/www.manifold.security\/blog\/third-party-com-placeholder-clickfix"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6ab524f82bf3c05dfa346cb8","name":"OpenSUpdater Hides in Recompiled 7zip SFX, Evading Analysts","description":"Threat actors are recompiling open source software, specifically the 7zip self-extracting archive stub, to embed a reflective loader that evades detection. The malicious code is inserted into the ExtractArchive function of the 7zip SFX module, making it difficult for analysts to identify since they typically focus on configuration files and embedded executables rather than the decompression stub itself. Samples are validly signed by Animated Productions, LLC and contain legitimate installers like foobar2000. The loader beacons to C2 servers, downloads DLLs, and reflectively loads encrypted payloads. Variants also abuse other open source libraries like the NSIS plugin EmbedHtml. Files feature bloated certificates and suspicious characteristics including installers wrapped within installers, requiring persistent analysis to uncover the hidden malicious functionality.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-09-24T19:45:27.898000","created":"2026-09-24T13:26:16.070000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4074171017,"indicator":"codeonicinc.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-09-24T13:26:16","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4479443725,"indicator":"setupsoftwarecenter.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-09-24T13:26:16","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4507053289,"indicator":"a7666e5aa3c6ecae0295caa7c3f49714eb561d6e1be6807cf1020b79f1902cd0","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-09-24T13:26:16","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4507053290,"indicator":"ba38916e82c47cff6de71791f179ce762e640e2975e40d6a1803d16ff591b752","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-09-24T13:26:16","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4507053291,"indicator":"e99a053b9d6a414256177e1529417f85867d6ed355f6009300d626f63429753c","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-09-24T13:26:16","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["7zip sfx","nsis","opensupdater","evasion techniques","snackarcin","reflective loader","code signing abuse","certificate bloating"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":["OpenSUpdater","Snackarcin"],"attack_ids":["T1036.005","T1204.002","T1553.002","T1140","T1036","T1027.001","T1059","T1547.001","T1027","T1573","T1071.001","T1105"],"references":["https:\/\/blog.gdatasoftware.com\/2026\/09\/38490-opensupdater-evades-with-recompiled-7zip-sfx"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6ab51a43ec94931b637c0607","name":"Konni Hackers Target Ukraine With Malicious LNK Files and VelvetCake PowerShell Malware","description":"North Korea-linked threat actors are conducting Operation Conflict Compass, targeting individuals and organizations focused on Ukraine using spear-phishing emails with malicious ZIP attachments. These contain LNK files disguised as PDFs with themes related to Russia-Ukraine peace plans, Ukrainian research, and geopolitical issues. When executed, the shortcuts retrieve malicious files from GitHub, deploying VBScript to establish persistence via scheduled tasks and delivering VelvetCake, a lightweight PowerShell-based task runner. VelvetCake contacts command-and-control infrastructure to download and execute additional scripts that perform reconnaissance, collect system information, enumerate security software, and capture screenshots. The campaign also utilized trojanized Zoom installers and leveraged infrastructure in South Korea and Ukraine, with activity observed since early August 2026 targeting diplomatic entities, think tanks, and NGOs.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-09-24T19:40:42.046000","created":"2026-09-24T12:40:35.284000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"Opal Sleet","indicators":[{"id":4503562613,"indicator":"p1o2i3u4y5t6r7e8w9q0.medianewsonline.com","type":"hostname","created":"2026-09-24T12:40:36","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4503562615,"indicator":"111.92.246.145","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-09-24T19:40:42","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-10-24T00:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["operation conflict compass","scheduled tasks","ukraine targeting","lnk files","north korea","spear-phishing","velvetcake","powershell"],"targeted_countries":["Ukraine"],"malware_families":["VelvetCake"],"attack_ids":[],"references":["https:\/\/cyberpress.org\/konni-targets-ukraine-with-velvetcake\/"],"industries":["Government","NGO"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6ab51a6d40cabb350f8e954b","name":"New RemControl Android Banking Trojan Steals PINs Using AI-Built Phishing Overlays","description":"RemControl is an Android banking trojan first observed in July 2026 that targets financial institutions across Western Europe, the Middle East, and Canada. The malware is distributed through fake Google Play Store pages advertising TVTap, an IPTV application, using malvertising campaigns with geo-targeted delivery. Once installed, the dropper creates a local VPN to block Play Protect checks and generates unique signing certificates per installation. RemControl exploits Android Accessibility Service permissions to display phishing overlays for over 30 banking applications, capturing PINs, mobile banking codes, and card details. The malware includes remote control capabilities, screen streaming, keylogging, and lock-screen pattern capture. It operates as Malware-as-a-Service with infrastructure showing evidence of AI-assisted development in phishing page creation and documentation.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-09-24T19:32:59.928000","created":"2026-09-24T12:41:17.021000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4505338142,"indicator":"vpn.doneplay.site","type":"hostname","created":"2026-09-24T12:41:17","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["android trojan","ai-assisted development","phishing overlays","websocket c2","accessibility service abuse","banking credentials","maas","remcontrol","tvtap"],"targeted_countries":["Canada","Italy"],"malware_families":["RemControl"],"attack_ids":["T1036","T1571","T1573"],"references":["https:\/\/cyberpress.org\/remcontrol-trojan-steals-banking-pins\/?amp=1"],"industries":["Finance"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6ab51a6bd938b813a0c50c5c","name":"TASK#STOMP PowerShell Backdoor Steals Business Documents and Maintains Persistent Remote Access","description":"A sophisticated PowerShell-based backdoor named TASK#STOMP has been discovered that specifically targets business documents while maintaining persistent remote access to compromised systems. The infection begins with VBScript execution, establishing persistence through scheduled tasks and startup folder entries. The malware deploys two primary PowerShell payloads that scan fixed drives for Word, PDF, PowerPoint, Excel, and archive files modified within the past year, excluding files larger than 500MB. It employs filesystem watchers for continuous collection of new documents. Additional capabilities include screenshot capture, Wi-Fi password theft, clipboard monitoring, and arbitrary command execution. The backdoor communicates with two command-and-control domains and uses compiled C helpers to bypass TLS certificate validation, enabling connections to servers with invalid certificates.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-09-24T19:31:04.466000","created":"2026-09-24T12:41:15.303000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4503138216,"indicator":"corecloudfileshare.xyz","type":"domain","created":"2026-09-24T12:41:16","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4503138217,"indicator":"attachmentsharingdrive.xyz","type":"domain","created":"2026-09-24T12:41:16","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["scheduled tasks","data exfiltration","avisloader","vbscript","task#stomp","tls bypass","powershell backdoor","velvetcake","document theft","filesystem monitoring","persistent access"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":["TASK#STOMP","VelvetCake","AvisLoader"],"attack_ids":["T1053.005","T1113","T1036.005","T1555.001","T1119","T1115","T1005","T1140","T1055","T1112","T1083","T1041","T1059.001","T1547.001","T1027","T1573.002","T1564.003","T1071.001","T1059.005","T1105"],"references":["https:\/\/cyberpress.org\/taskstomp-backdoor-steals-documents\/?amp=1"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6ab51a418ee0b2466a9da4f1","name":"Galago Ransomware Emerges With Shared Infrastructure Ties to Panzer","description":"Galago is a newly identified ransomware operation that emerged in September 2026, claiming operational partnership with the Panzer ransomware group. The connection is suggested through shared infrastructure, specifically matching prefixes in their Tor leak-site addresses (pnzr4del for Galago and pnzruro for Panzer). Galago was first detected following an alleged attack on an Icelandic healthcare organization on 9 September 2026, though this claim remains unverified as their dark leak site showed no published victims. Panzer, described as a ransomware-as-a-service operation, has published 32 victims between August and September 2026 and employs double extortion tactics. While the naming pattern and self-reported claims suggest a relationship, no independent evidence confirms shared operators, malware, or infrastructure control between the two groups.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-09-24T19:25:28.661000","created":"2026-09-24T12:40:33.724000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"Galago","indicators":[{"id":4474373998,"indicator":"pnzruro7syvwvefx5mpo2fhzi4jftgquynsqf3vy5x3no57yp2iz4nyd.onion","type":"domain","created":"2026-09-24T12:40:34","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4496728505,"indicator":"pnzr4delgur5dlhtqcy7qqm6m7dkivxwh742enezpks5kswfpx7qrsid.onion","type":"domain","created":"2026-09-24T12:40:34","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["healthcare targeting","double extortion","tor leak site","iceland","raas","infrastructure sharing","galago","ransomware","panzer"],"targeted_countries":["Iceland"],"malware_families":["Galago","Panzer"],"attack_ids":["T1133","T1489","T1071","T1005","T1562","T1567","T1552","T1589","T1021","T1090","T1070","T1083","T1041","T1210","T1048","T1566","T1078","T1486","T1490"],"references":["https:\/\/cyberpress.org\/galago-ransomware-linked-to-panzer\/?amp=1"],"industries":["Healthcare"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6ab5176a22ab1049d0969c4a","name":"A new version of the MacSync macOS stealer targets crypto enthusiasts and developers","description":"A detailed technical analysis examines the evolution of MacSync, a macOS stealer-as-a-service initially known as Mac.c, which targets cryptocurrency enthusiasts and developers. The malware has undergone significant changes, replacing AppleScript-based droppers with binary executable files written in Objective-C and Swift. The infection chain utilizes malicious DMG images and employs iCloud infrastructure for payload delivery. MacSync collects extensive data including browser credentials, cryptocurrency wallets, Telegram data, SSH configurations, and keychain files. The stealer incorporates novel techniques like PAM API for password verification and features a backdoor module for persistent access. Distribution occurs through social engineering, fake applications, and cracked software disguised as legitimate crypto wallets like the nonexistent Toria wallet, promoted through dedicated websites and social media channels.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-09-24T19:23:16.583000","created":"2026-09-24T12:28:26.758000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4506997203,"indicator":"26a0f7cdb9f7dc5ace9a40af825b1538","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-09-24T12:28:27","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4506997204,"indicator":"2d69812584269699fade26622e6490c5","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-09-24T12:28:27","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4506997205,"indicator":"7df1049cbd56c0bfa4a3364a379b4c2c","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-09-24T12:28:27","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4506997206,"indicator":"9f15fe9c4415cd668334339f705b94d8","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-09-24T12:28:27","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4506997207,"indicator":"fb90887592655a8c989e443c640167aa","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-09-24T12:28:27","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4506997208,"