allel activities: distribution of trojanized cryptocurrency wallet applications and a botnet infrastructure. The botnet leverages Hermes Agent, an MIT-licensed open-source AI framework, modified with a custom prompt directing it to execute commands via Telegram, maintain persistence, and harvest credentials. The campaign infrastructure spans multiple hosting providers including Linode, Hetzner, and Contabo, with activity documented from October 2024 through August 2026.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-09-24T07:57:47.370000","created":"2026-09-24T07:56:13.523000","revision":3,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":71681052,"indicator":"213.136.79.115","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-09-24T07:56:14","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-10-24T07:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":71681052,"indicator":"213.136.79.115","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-09-24T07:57:35","content":"","title":"","description":"CC=DE ASN=AS51167 contabo gmbh","expiration":"2026-10-24T07:00:00","is_active":1,"role":"scanning_host"},{"id":4451373518,"indicator":"190.211.124.187","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-09-24T07:56:14","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-10-24T07:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4451373518,"indicator":"190.211.124.187","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-09-24T07:57:35","content":"","title":"","description":"CC=CR ASN=AS262145 cooperativa de electrificacin rural de san carlos r.l. (coopelesca r.l.)","expiration":"2026-10-24T07:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4506924635,"indicator":"91.99.195.164","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-09-24T07:57:35","content":"","title":"","description":"CC=IR ASN=AS16322 pars online pjs","expiration":"2026-10-24T07:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["cryptocurrency","credential theft","telegram","botnet","ai framework","carbonato","docker","hermes agent","container security","exposed daemon"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":["CARBONATO","Hermes Agent"],"attack_ids":["T1543","T1133","T1071","T1053","T1140","T1190","T1555","T1567","T1219","T1552","T1090","T1102","T1204","T1072","T1027","T1573","T1132","T1111","T1136","T1105"],"references":["https:\/\/www.threatdown.com\/blog\/carbonato\/"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a8d406a23f75e32b69c2029","name":"Tracking PavinLoader across ClickFix and fake download campaigns","description":"A sophisticated multi-stage loader dubbed PavinLoader has been identified across multiple distribution campaigns including ClickFix attacks, fake software downloads, and malicious RenPy games. The loader employs heavily obfuscated .NET DLLs, abuses legitimate Windows tools like MSBuild, and utilizes EtherHiding technique to retrieve command-and-control domains via blockchain. The infection chain consists of four main stages: a Loader DLL performing anti-forensics, an EtherHiding Loader obtaining C2 infrastructure, an Anti-Analysis DLL checking for virtualized environments, and a PE Loader delivering final payloads including Amatera Stealer. Evidence suggests PavinLoader may be offered as a Loader-as-a-Service, with common artifacts found across over 200 related files. The campaigns demonstrate sophisticated evasion techniques including custom obfuscation, API hashing, and extensive anti-analysis checks targeting virtualized environments and specific geographic regions.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-09-24T07:01:08.453000","created":"2026-08-25T07:12:42.005000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4271644414,"indicator":"more-arpc.icu","type":"domain","created":"2026-08-25T07:12:42","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4271644415,"indicator":"rpcsecnoweb.pro","type":"domain","created":"2026-08-25T07:12:42","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4363821584,"indicator":"kelemet.shop","t